{"name":"Platinum","hex":"#e5e4e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"platinum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The chemical element with atomic number 78 and symbol Pt; a dense, malleable, ductile, highly unreactive, silverish-white transition metal of great value.","A whitish grey colour, like that of the metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a whitish grey colour, like that of the metal.","Of a musical recording that has sold over one million copies (for singles), or two million (for albums)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platinum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Platinum","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum is a chemical element; it has symbol Pt and atomic number 78. It is a dense, malleable, ductile, highly unreactive, precious, silverish-white transition metal. Its name originates from Spanish platina, a diminutive of plata \"silver\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Platinum_crystals.jpg/330px-Platinum_crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum","wikidata":"Q880"},{"title":"Platinum (Mike Oldfield album)","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum is the fifth studio album by English multi-instrumentalist and songwriter Mike Oldfield, released on 23 November 1979 on Virgin Records. It was Oldfield's first album to include shorter songs and music written by others. A modified version of the album was released in the United States and Canada and titled Airborn."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Mike_oldfield_platinum_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum_(Mike_Oldfield_album)","wikidata":"Q929074"},{"title":"Platinum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum is a color that is the metallic tint of pale grayish-white resembling the metal platinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/